                  <msItem>
                     <title>T. de Eccleston, etc.</title>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Formerly London, The Robinson Trust (Phillipps
                        3119, fols. 55--121).</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">For this copy see N. R. Ker in BLR 6 (1959), p.
                        491, and id., Books, Collectors and Libraries, pp. 411 &amp; 435.</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">See A. G. Little, 'Tractatus fratris Thomae de
                        Eccleston', Collection d'Etudes et de Documents VII (1909), pp. xiii--xvii.
                        Evidently the MS. referred to by Bale as being at Queen's Coll., Oxford (see
                        Index, pp. 473, 378, 437, 238 for arts. 14, 21--23, 27--30 in the table of
                        contents printed by Little.</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Chainmark on fol. 55r, near foot.</note>
                  </msItem>
               </msContents>
               <history>
                  <origin>
                     <origDate when-custom="1250/1400" notBefore="1250" notAfter="1400" calendar="#gregorian">s. xiii ex.--xiv ex.</origDate>
                  </origin>
                  <provenance><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_439">Oxford, Oxfordshire. The Queen's
                        College</orgName><p>(fol. 56r) '7vo'.</p><note type="MLGB3_medievalCatalogueNotes">Cf. Bale, Index, p. 238,
                     etc.</note></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Bale, who owned also the other parts of the
                     MS. (see H. McCusker, 'Books and MSS. in the possession of John Bale', Trans.
                     Bibl. Soc. 16 (1935), nos. 48--49, 133, 170--173.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Bale's hand occurs on many leaves and a slip
                     inserted after fol. 86 is in his writing.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Page-Turner (Bettlesden) sale 19 Oct. 1824
                     lot 2716/2 to Phillipps. '2716/2' is on fol. 1r.</provenance>
               </history>
